   178	basis of $A(W)$ on $\{\Delta^{-1}<\Delta<a<b\}$ consists of the 8 relations
   179	$$\begin{aligned}
   180	&R_1:\ \langle ab\rangle_m\to\Delta,\quad R_2:\ \langle ba\rangle_m\to\Delta,\\
   181	&R_3^x:\ x\Delta\to\Delta\varphi(x),\quad R_4^x:\ x\Delta^{-1}\to\Delta^{-1}\varphi(x)\quad(x\in\{a,b\}),\\
   182	&R_5:\ \Delta\Delta^{-1}\to1,\quad R_6:\ \Delta^{-1}\Delta\to1,
   183	\end{aligned}$$
   184	$\varphi=\mathrm{id}$ for $m$ even, $\varphi=(a\,b)$ for $m$ odd. The normal forms are
   185	$\Delta^{(k)}w$, $w\in\{a,b\}^*$ without alternating factor of length $m$ (= Garside normal form).
   186	For rank 1 ($A_1$, $N=1$, $\Delta=a$) the reduced basis is $\{a\to\Delta,\Delta\Delta^{-1}\to1,\Delta^{-1}\Delta\to1\}$.
