   196	1. $R_i/R_j$, $i,j\in\{1,2\}$: a proper suffix of an alternating word is a prefix of an alternating
   197	   word iff their letters agree, so $w$ is an alternating word of length $m+j$, $1\le j\le m-1$.
   198	   Write $w=w'\,\bar g=\bar f\,w''$ with $|w'|=|w''|=j$. Then $w\to\Delta w''$ and
   199	   $w\to w'\Delta\to^*\Delta\varphi(w')$ by $j$ applications of $R_3$. Positions $i$ and $i+m$ of an
   200	   alternating word carry the same letter iff $m$ is even, so $w''=\varphi(w')$: joinable.
