   207	5. $R_4/R_6$: symmetric to 4.
   208	6. $R_5/R_6$, $R_6/R_5$: $\Delta\Delta^{-1}\Delta\to\Delta$ both ways; $\Delta^{-1}\Delta\Delta^{-1}\to\Delta^{-1}$ both ways.
   209	
   210	These are all overlaps: suffixes of leading words that are prefixes of leading words are a letter
   211	$x$ (suffix of $R_{1,2}$; prefixes of $R_{1,2},R_3^x,R_4^x$), $\Delta$ (suffix of $R_3,R_6$; prefix
