   323	For a trim deterministic automaton: if some strongly connected component contains a vertex with
   324	two internal out-edges, the number of accepted words of length $L$ grows exponentially (two
   325	distinct cycles at a vertex give $2^k$ distinct paths, hence words, of equal length); otherwise
   326	every cyclic SCC is a simple cycle and the count is $O(L^{d-1})$ and $\ge cL^{d-1}$ along an
   327	arithmetic progression, $d$ the maximal number of cyclic SCCs on a path (choose independent
   328	repetition counts of the $d$ cycles). Applying this to the exact pair automaton of Theorem B
   329	(`work/classify.py`, trimmed to co-accessible states) gives, for the positive part of the reduced
   330	GS basis (and identically for the monoid basis, option `--monoid`):
   331	
   332	| type | orders with polynomial growth (degree) | all other orders |
   333	|---|---|---|
   334	| $I_2(m)$ | all: finite (Theorem C) | — |
   335	| $A_3$ | middle node largest (2 orders): degree 1 | exponential |
   336	| $B_3$ | $s_1<s_3<s_2$: degree 1; $s_3<s_1<s_2$: degree 2 | exponential |
   337	| $H_3$ ($s_1\overset5—s_2—s_3$) | $s_1<s_3<s_2$: degree 3; $s_3<s_1<s_2$: degree 2 | exponential |
   338	| $D_4$ | centre largest (6 orders): degree 4 | exponential |
   339	| $A_4,B_4,F_4,H_4$ | none | exponential (all 24 orders) |
   340	
   341	By Lemma 3, $P(W)\supseteq\mathrm{MinRed}(A^+_J)$ for every proper parabolic $J$; the monoid
