    29	   The braid group Bn+1 for the Euclidean space consisting on n + 1 strands is
    30	given by the following Artin presentation [3]:
    31	                *                                                             +
    32	                                   zi zj = zj zi if | i − j | ≥ 2
    33	       Bn+1 = z1 , z2 , . . . , zn                                              .
    34	                                   zi+1 zi zi+1 = zi zi+1 zi if 1 ≤ i ≤ n − 1
    35	Elements of Bn+1 are expressed in the generators z1 , z2 , . . . , zn and their inverses.
    36	The presentation of the braid monoid MBn+1 is similar to the presentation of
    37	Bn+1 . In [12] Lambropoulou gave the presentation of the mixed braid monoid
    38	Bm,n . Before this presentation she gave the presentation of B1,n in [11]. In this
    39	paper we compute the Hilbert series of B1,3 .
    40	Definition 1.1 ([12]). The mixed braid group Bm,n of m + n strands is defined as
    41	              *                       βr βs = βs βr if |r − s| ≥ 2               +
    42	                  α1 , . . . , αm ,   βr+1 βr βr+1 = βr βr+1 βr if 1 ≤ r ≤ n − 1
