    32	| **(1) General Coxeter groups; Bokut–Shiao conjecture** | **partially solved** | The original conjectural formula is **false**, not still an unrefuted conjecture: Chen–Liu [CL09], Example 3.2, gives a four-generator counterexample in standard involutive generators with degree-lex `s1<s2<s3<s4`; their replacement pre-GS conjecture is proved only under stated restrictions. Explicit finite-type results include Lee–Lee [LL19] for H2/H3/H4 (standard reflection generators, degree-lex increasing indices), and Pang–Wang [PW26] for G2/F4/E6/E7/E8 (degree-lex, their relabeled Coxeter diagrams). The latter authors state that this completes their finite irreducible list; this does **not** settle an explicit uniform basis for arbitrary Coxeter matrices. Ustaoğlu [US24] treats affine B/D in standard involutive generators and degree-lex. All these PDFs were opened. |
