   100	## C. Important source-reading qualifications
   101	
   102	### The 2014 survey is not a current blanket nonexistence theorem
   103	
   104	**L. A. Bokut and Yuqun Chen**, *Gröbner–Shirshov bases and their calculation*, *Bulletin of Mathematical Sciences* 4 (2014), 325–395, [arXiv:1303.5366](https://arxiv.org/abs/1303.5366), [DOI:10.1007/s13373-014-0054-6](https://doi.org/10.1007/s13373-014-0054-6). **Opened PDF**, particularly introduction and §3.1.
   105	
   106	- Local text lines 550–553 say: “Artin–Tits groups ... GS bases are not known except for braid groups (the Artin–Tits groups of type A_n).” This is a historical generalization, not adequate as a 2026 verdict: [BV06] covers all rank two in changed generators, and the survey itself cites [CZ13], whose §3 treats type B.
   107	- §3.1 distinguishes Artin–Burau, Artin–Garside, BKL, and Adjan/Adyan–Thurston alphabets. Theorem 3.2 explicitly uses inverse-tower order; §3.1.2 explicitly uses `Delta^{-1}<Delta<sigma1<...<sigman` degree-lex.
   108	- The introduction's broad finite-Coxeter sentence should not be used to assign priority for E8/H4; newer primary papers and earlier thesis citations are more precise.
   109	
   110	### Two published claimed bases with visible inverse-overlap concerns
   111	
   112	These are **[INFERENCE] from the displayed relations and the specified degree-lex order**, not a published erratum, not a full proof audit, and not a machine verification. They are recorded to avoid promoting a paper's theorem heading to a certified solution.
   113	
   114	1. **[KO20], Theorem 2.1, pp.934–935.** It lists the positive rule `mu23 mu13 mu12 -> mu12 mu13 mu23` and cancellation `mu12 mu12^{-1}->1`. The overlap word
   115	   `mu23 mu13 mu12 mu12^{-1}`
   116	   has the two reducts `mu23 mu13` and `mu12 mu13 mu23 mu12^{-1}`. For the displayed list (1)–(26), the former has length two with no inverse pair; the latter has no listed positive leading triple, no longer positive leading word, and no cancellation. Thus they appear distinct irreducibles. The paper lists this overlap among ambiguities but does not display its reduction to zero. This needs repair/independent checking before the displayed system is relied upon.
   117	2. **[KOC19], Theorem 3.2, p.81.** The displayed noncancellation rules are positive, including `sts->tst` (`u>s>t`), and the remaining rules cancel inverse pairs. The overlap `sts s^{-1}` reduces either to `st` or to `tst s^{-1}`; neither contains a displayed leading positive rule or inverse cancellation. This is the same structural issue. The paper's presentation is of the complex braid group, unlike [CA20], but its claimed group basis still cannot be accepted here without resolving this issue.
   118	
   119	These cautions do not claim the word problems themselves are unsolvable, nor that no corrected basis exists.
   120	
   121	## D. Later surveys, 2020 book, citation chains, and standard-generator automaticity
   122	
   123	### D1. Later Bokut/Chen material and the 2020 monograph
   124	
   125	1. **Bokut–Chen, *Gröbner–Shirshov bases and PBW theorems***, [arXiv:1502.06472](https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.06472). **Opened abstract and PDF.** §5 lists braid normal forms in Artin–Burau, Artin–Garside, BKL and Adyan–Thurston generators, citing the familiar papers. It does not supply a new non-A atom-plus-Delta theorem. The document has a 2014 datestamp; Chen's 2018 CV records the related journal paper in *Journal of Siberian Federal University, Mathematics and Physics* 6(4) (2013), 417–427. The later arXiv identifier is not evidence of a new 2015 solution.
   126	2. **L. A. Bokut, Yuqun Chen and Abdukadir Obul**, *Some new results on Gröbner–Shirshov bases for Lie algebras and around*, *International Journal of Algebra and Computation* 28(8) (2018), 1403–1423, [DOI:10.1142/S0218196718400027](https://doi.org/10.1142/S0218196718400027). **Opened publisher-supplied abstract via DOI/Crossref; full text not opened.** Its stated scope is Lie, operated Lie, Gelfand–Dorfman–Novikov, Leibniz, and extension results. No Artin-group update is stated in that abstract; **the full paper's Artin status discussion is [UNVERIFIED]**.
   127	3. The similarly titled *Gröbner–Shirshov Bases: Some New Results* (Bokut–Chen, [arXiv:0804.1344](https://arxiv.org/abs/0804.1344)) and *Some new results on Gröbner–Shirshov bases* (Bokut–Chen–Shum, [arXiv:1102.0449](https://arxiv.org/abs/1102.0449)) are **older leads**, not 2014–2026 updates. Their full mathematical texts were not opened here: **[UNVERIFIED]**. Chen's opened 2018 CV dates the latter proceedings version to 2012, pp.53–102.
   128	4. **Leonid Bokut, Yuqun Chen, Kyriakos Kalorkoti, Pavel Kolesnikov and Viktor Lopatkin**, *Gröbner–Shirshov Bases: Normal Forms, Combinatorial and Decision Problems in Algebra*, World Scientific (2020), 308 pp., [DOI:10.1142/9287](https://doi.org/10.1142/9287), ISBN 9789814619486 / 9789814619509. **Opened author-institution description, Google Play book page, and an actual Google Books preview/TOC** ([book ID GmjvDwAAQBAJ](https://books.google.com/books?id=GmjvDwAAQBAJ&printsec=frontcover)).
   129	   - The author-institution and Google Play descriptions mention the **Artin–Markov braid normal form in Burau generators**, not a theorem for non-A Artin–Tits groups.
